{"body":"Found while fixing #138 in the UNIFIED_INGREDIENT_MAPPING builder\n(culturebotai-claw). Measured over `data/ingredients/mapped/*.yaml` on\n2026-09-06; numbers, not recollection.\n\n## Measurement\n\n```\nmapped records                                   2,678\ncarrying kg_microbe_node_id                        376\nkg_microbe_node_id ≠ identifier                     51\n  same prefix (a contradictory \"corrected\" column)  29   ← 2,400 occurrences\n  cross prefix                                      22\n```\n\nThe same-prefix 29, by occurrences:\n\n| record | identifier | kg_microbe_node_id | occ |\n|---|---|---|---:|\n| `Coso4_X_7_H2o` | `CHEBI:91244` (heptahydrate) | `CHEBI:53470` (anhydrous) | 828 |\n| `Edta` | `CHEBI:4735` (free acid) | `CHEBI:64755` (EDTA(2−)) | 569 |\n| `Na2hpo4_X_2_H2o` | `CHEBI:91258` | `CHEBI:34683` | 304 |\n| `Hepes` | `CHEBI:42334` | `CHEBI:46756` | 251 |\n| `Thiamine` | `CHEBI:18385` | `CHEBI:26948` | 159 |\n| `Na2hpo4_X_12_H2o` | `CHEBI:91259` | `CHEBI:34683` | 159 |\n| `Fructose` | `CHEBI:28757` | `CHEBI:28645` | 87 |\n| `Thiamine_pyrophosphate` | `CHEBI:9532` | `CHEBI:18290` | 26 |\n\nEvery one is a MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 correction — hydration state, free acid\nvs anion, specific vs generic — applied to `identifier` while\n`kg_microbe_node_id` stayed on the id it superseded. The record asserts two\nidentities at once.\n\n## Why it is #138's problem one column over\n\n`kg_microbe_node_id` flows verbatim into `UNIFIED_INGREDIENT_MAPPING.tsv`, and\nkg-microbe reads it. Two consequences, both already live:\n\n1. **Its corrected-first ranker prefers the stale value.** kg-microbe#723 added\n   `corrected_column_primary([kg_node_id, mim_id, chebi_id, culturemech_term,\n   cas])` to report divergences — `kg_node_id` first. For these 29 rows that\n   path grounds to the superseded id and reports MIM's actual `identifier` as\n   the disagreement. The \"corrected\" column is the one that is wrong.\n2. **It masks the #138 mechanism in analysis.** Any TSV-level check that treats\n   `mim_id`/`kg_microbe_node_id` as \"MIM's answer\" sees them disagree and cannot\n   tell which is stale. It fooled mine: I under-counted #138's blast radius by 5\n   rows (HEPES, TPP, CMC…) until I compared against `identifier` alone.\n\nThe builder fix for #138 (claw PR, in flight) deliberately keys precedence on\n`mim_id` = `identifier`, so the published `chebi_id`/`culturemech_term_id` are\nnow right for these rows — but `kg_microbe_node_id` still ships the\ncontradiction, because the builder copies the record field and correcting\nrecord data is not a builder's job.\n\n## What I did not do\n\nNot touched in the #138 PR: this is record curation, 29 records, and each\ncorrection should append a `curation_history` event. Nor did I infer which\nside is right by rule — every case I looked at favours `identifier`, and the\n§3 pattern says the same, but that is what a curation pass is for.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nA one-off pass that, for records where `kg_microbe_node_id` and `identifier`\nshare a prefix and differ, sets `kg_microbe_node_id = identifier` with a\nhistory event citing this issue — plus a `qc-duplicate-ids`-style invariant so\na future §3 correction to `identifier` cannot leave the sibling field behind\nagain. The 22 cross-prefix cases (e.g. a CHEBI identifier with a FOODON node\nid) may be legitimate dual-classification and want a look, not a rule.","comments":[],"number":554,"state":"CLOSED","title":"29 records publish a kg_microbe_node_id that contradicts their own identifier (2,400 occurrences) — the corrected-first ranker would pick the stale one","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/554"}
